    [Performance][EPLB] Make log2phy map commits asynchronous (#18020)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Make the EPLB log2phy map commit asynchronous. Convert CPU planner maps
    to the destination dtype in pinned memory, then copy with
    `non_blocking=True` to avoid draining queued NPU work on the host.
    
    Backport: #19366.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No API or configuration changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `bash format.sh ci`: passed.
    - Real Ascend NPU experiments verified asynchronous map copies,
    pinned-source lifetime, and eager/graph consumption with HCCL ordering.
    The validation scripts are kept outside this PR.
    - Temporary NPU validation on the simplified commit: 4 checks passed. No
    test files are added by this PR. Full model accuracy and throughput were
    not measured.
    
    - Existing CPU tests with Ascend runtime stubs: 76 passed. GitHub
    pre-commit, both CPU test jobs, and the CI gate passed on commit
    `6883ab0bd6263268f28bbdb2496146aa96348904`.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    Signed-off-by: freyfwt <freytian1996@gmail.com>

